<div class="faq-section">
  <!-- Student Q&A --> <h2 data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>Student Q&A: Aviation & Aerospace After PUC</h2>
  
<details class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <summary data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>Is CPL worth the ₹40L+ investment?</summary> <div class="faq-answer" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <p data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>
Only if: (1) You've passed DGCA Class 1 medical pre-check, (2) You have backup capital for type ratings + living expenses during job search, (3) You're okay with 2–4 years of uncertain hiring cycles. Many students pivot to AME or aviation management after realizing CPL ROI is volatile.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <summary data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>Do I really need to relocate for training?</summary> <div class="faq-answer" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <p data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>
For pilot/AME paths: yes, most DGCA-approved institutes are outside Karnataka. For aerospace engineering/airport ops: Bangalore has opportunities (HAL, ISRO, BLR Airport). Factor relocation costs (₹1L–₹3L/year) into your budget.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <summary data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>What if I fail DGCA medical after paying fees?</summary> <div class="faq-answer" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <p data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>
This is why we emphasize <strong data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>pre-checkup before payment</strong>. If disqualification happens post-enrollment, most institutes offer partial refunds or course transfers (e.g., pilot to aviation management). Read refund policies carefully before signing.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <summary data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>Can I switch from engineering to pilot training later?</summary> <div class="faq-answer" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <p data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>
Yes, but you'll still need to complete full CPL training (₹40L+) and clear DGCA medical. Your engineering degree won't reduce flying hours or licensing requirements. Better to decide early to avoid duplicate investment.
</p> </div> </details>
<details class="faq-item" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <summary data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>How do I get internships at MROs or airports?</summary> <div class="faq-answer" data-astro-cid-ug7vciio> <p data-astro-cid-ug7vciio>
Start by Semester 2 of AME/aviation management programs. Email MROs/airports with clear interest, attach your PUC/B.Tech transcript + 1 mini-project/certification, apply via DGCA/IATA portals, and use C2 Club to find open slots. Cold outreach works if your email is specific, not generic.
</p> </div> </details>
